---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {
  ADSENSE_CMP_CONFIGURED,
  ADSENSE_CONFIGURED,
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
} from '../data/site-config';

const privacyDescription =
  'What happens to the files you process on Kit-Bin, what data is and isn\'t collected, how HilltopAds advertising and consent choices work, and your GDPR rights.';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Kit-Bin"
  description={privacyDescription}
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 space-y-6 text-ink dark:text-slate-300">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-slate-100">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted dark:text-slate-500">Last updated: 25 August 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Your files</h2>
      <p>
        Every tool on this site currently processes files entirely in your browser, using
        WebAssembly and native browser APIs. Your file is read into your browser's memory, the
        conversion runs on your device, and the result downloads directly to your device. At no
        point is a file you select uploaded to any server. This applies to every tool currently
        live on the site. None of them use a server fallback. If that changes for a specific
        tool in the future (for very large files or a format that genuinely can't be processed
        client-side), that tool's own page will say so explicitly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Accounts and storage</h2>
      <p>
        There are no user accounts on this site. Files you select or process are not uploaded to
        or stored on Kit-Bin servers, and Kit-Bin does not maintain a database of user files.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not currently run any analytics or tracking script. If aggregate,
        cookieless usage analytics (page views, general device/location category, not
        individual tracking) are added in the future, this section will be updated to say so
        before that happens.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="advertising">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Kit-Bin shows a small number of standard banner advertisements, served by HilltopAds, to
        help cover hosting and development costs. These are static banner ads, not video, not
        audio, and not a full-screen interstitial. They never appear inside a file drop area or in
        a way that could be mistaken for part of a tool.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        After a tool finishes processing your file, and only if you have accepted advertising
        cookies, the download button is covered by a short 10-second panel showing a gradient
        countdown ring and one video advertisement, also served by HilltopAds, before the button
        becomes clickable. This is the one place on the site a video ad is shown — everywhere
        else, ads are the static banners described above. Your file is never reprocessed or held
        back during this wait; it was already finished before the countdown started, and the
        10-second wait itself runs on a fixed timer independent of the video, so a slow or
        unavailable ad never extends it. If you have declined advertising cookies, or have not yet
        chosen, this step does not happen at all and the download button is available immediately.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Once you click that download button to take your finished file, and only if you have
        accepted advertising cookies, a single additional HilltopAds advertisement opens in a new
        background browser tab. This happens once per visit, only from that click, and only after
        your file is already downloading — never during upload, processing, or the countdown
        described above.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        None of HilltopAds' advertising resources are requested at all until you accept the cookie
        banner shown on your first visit. If you decline, or before you choose either way, no
        advertising script or advertising cookie loads, and every tool continues to work exactly
        the same either way. You can change your choice at any time using{' '}
        <strong>Privacy and cookie settings</strong> in the footer, which also removes any advertising
        already loaded on the page.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Once loaded, HilltopAds and its advertising partners may use cookies, pixels, or similar
        technologies for ad delivery, measurement, and fraud prevention, and where permitted,
        limited personalization. This is entirely separate from how your files are handled: the
        advertiser is never given a file's name, contents, or any conversion setting, because the
        advertising code has no access to the file-processing code at all. The banner ads run in
        an isolated frame. The download-gate video ad runs directly in a standard HTML video
        player rather than an isolated frame, since a video element requires direct access to the
        page to play — it only ever requests and plays a video ad, and is never given anything
        related to your file. The post-download advertisement opens in its own separate browser
        tab and has no access to this page at all.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        {ADSENSE_CONFIGURED ? (
          <>
            Kit-Bin also uses Google AdSense. Google may process information such as the page URL, IP
            address, browser information, and advertising identifiers to serve, measure, and protect
            advertising. See{' '}
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" class="underline">
              how Google uses information from sites that use its services
            </a>. {ADSENSE_CMP_CONFIGURED
              ? 'Privacy and cookie choices for AdSense are presented through the configured Google CMP.'
              : 'AdSense is configured but its Google CMP is not yet enabled, so personalized AdSense advertising is not served to UK, EEA, or Swiss visitors until that is in place.'}
          </>
        ) : (
          'Google AdSense is not active on Kit-Bin yet. This section will be updated with the details above before AdSense is enabled.'
        )}
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="cookies">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Kit-Bin itself sets no cookies. The site's own preferences (light/dark theme, your
        Favorites list, and your advertising consent choice) are stored using
        <code>localStorage</code> in your browser, not cookies, and are never sent to any server —
        Kit-Bin has no backend to send them to. If you accept advertising cookies, HilltopAds and
        its advertising partners may then set their own cookies or use similar technologies (see
        <strong> Advertising</strong> above) for ad delivery, measurement, and fraud prevention.
        Declining, in the cookie banner or later via <strong>Privacy and cookie settings</strong>
        in the footer, blocks those from ever being set and removes any that already were.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="gdpr">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">
        Your rights under GDPR (UK &amp; EEA visitors)
      </h2>
      <p>
        Kit-Bin is built to need as little of your personal data as possible: your files are
        processed entirely in your own browser and never uploaded (see <strong>Your files</strong>
        above), and the site runs no analytics or account system. The only personal data Kit-Bin's
        advertising can involve is what HilltopAds itself may collect — via cookies, pixels, or
        similar technologies — once you have actively opted in through the cookie banner, as
        described in <strong>Advertising</strong> above. Advertising is opt-in, not opt-out: no
        advertising cookie is set and no advertising request is made until you accept.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        If you are in the UK, EEA, or Switzerland, you have the right to: know what personal data
        is processed and why (this page); withdraw consent to advertising at any time, with
        immediate effect, via <strong>Privacy and cookie settings</strong> in the footer; request
        access to, correction of, or erasure of personal data that a third party such as HilltopAds
        holds about you, by contacting that provider directly, since Kit-Bin itself does not hold
        or store any profile about you; and lodge a complaint with your local data protection
        supervisory authority if you believe your rights have not been respected.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Because Kit-Bin never uploads, stores, or has a mechanism to identify the files you
        process, there is no file-related personal data for Kit-Bin to provide, correct, or erase
        on request — that data never reaches Kit-Bin in the first place. Requests about
        advertising data should go to HilltopAds directly, as Kit-Bin does not have access to or
        control over what that provider retains once an ad has been served.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="underline">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
